# Saturday Build Day — NEXUS Systems & Automation

**Saturdays are Build Day. Every Saturday, Dee builds the systems that make the weekdays faster. NEXUS supports accordingly.**

## The Weekly Structure

| Day | Focus | Rule |
|---|---|---|
| **Monday–Friday** | Revenue — calls, bids, outreach, proposals, follow-ups, closing | No building, no tinkering. Move money. |
| **Saturday** | Build — systems, code, automation, NEXUS upgrades | No outreach, no bids. Build the machine. |
| **Sunday** | GBIS — grants, community outreach, Cause We Care | Per `gbis-sunday-cadence.mdc` |

## What Happens Every Saturday

1. **Check the Build Queue** — Read `TODAY_AGENDA.md` for any scheduled Saturday builds
2. **Pick the Highest-Impact Build** — What will save the most time during the week?
3. **Build, Test, Deploy** — Code it, verify it works, push to production
4. **Document What Changed** — Update relevant docs so Monday's session knows what's new
5. **Git Commit & Push** — All code changes committed before end of session

## Build Categories (Pick One Per Saturday)

### NEXUS Platform
- Frontend dashboard improvements (React components, UX upgrades)
- Backend API endpoints (new features, performance fixes)
- AI Copilot upgrades (smarter responses, new capabilities)
- Airtable schema changes or new integrations
- Deploy updates to PythonAnywhere + Netlify

### Automation & Mining
- New mining scripts (opportunities, contacts, pricing)
- Scheduler improvements (cron jobs, automated alerts)
- RSS feed expansions
- Email automation

### PRISM / Field Service
- PRISM module build-out
- Field agent portal features
- BioChain QA gates
- Drug testing / DNA / fingerprinting workflow automation

### Integrations
- Alexa skill wiring
- Calendar automation (.ics generation)
- Airtable-to-frontend data flows
- API integrations with partners (Quest, NDS, etc.)

## Saturday Startup

When Dee opens Cursor on a Saturday:

1. **Check `TODAY_AGENDA.md`** for the scheduled build
2. If no build is scheduled: review the NEXUS backlog and propose the highest-impact item
3. Present: "Saturday Build Day. On the board: [scheduled build]. Ready to go?"
4. Dive straight into building — no outreach, no emails, no bids

## Rules for Build Day

- **No client outreach on Saturdays.** Build only. Revenue work stays on weekdays.
- **One major build per Saturday.** Don't scatter across 5 things. Pick one, finish it, ship it.
- **Test before deploy.** Every build gets tested locally before pushing to production.
- **Document the change.** A build that isn't documented doesn't exist for Monday's session.
- **Commit everything.** Git add, commit, push before the session ends.

## Why Saturdays

Weekdays are for generating revenue. Building systems during the week steals time from calls, bids, and outreach — the activities that put money in the door. Saturdays give Dee uninterrupted focus time to build without competing priorities. Every Saturday build compounds — the system gets smarter, the weekdays get faster, and DDI scales without adding headcount.

